    "narrative": "The Zebras\u2019 offensive outlook for May 15th centers on a high-ceiling performance from **Yordan Alvarez** (75.69), whose elite xwOBA of .421 and favorable matchup against Leiter make him the premier start. We are also capitalizing on the high-upside speed profile of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.53); while batting 8th generally suppresses value, his efficiency is spiked by a 14% platoon edge and a generous 87% stolen base success rate against a slow-moving Burke, keeping him firmly in the \"Strong\" category. **Junior Caminero** (67.27) rounds out our top-tier tier, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Junk allows him to overcome a neutral park factor and provide stable production in the heart of our lineup.\n\nEfficiency concerns persist with **Trea Turner** (53.83) and **Kyle Schwarber** (52.46), both of whom face a stiff test against the 3.52 xERA of Ashcraft. While **Trea Turner** remains locked in due to his leadoff spot and stolen base potential, his raw projection is dampened by the high skill of the opposing arm. On the bubble, **Chase Meidroth** (44.54) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine. While his base projection was respectable, the optimizer favored the platoon leverage provided by **Luke Raley** (59.77) and the speed-dependent utility of **Hyeseong Kim** (59.19) against Kochanowicz. We continue to monitor the status of **Lars Nootbaar** and **Zac Veen**, but with both currently sidelined by injury or minor league assignment, our depth remains tested. Caution is advised regarding **Dillon Dingler**, who faces a suboptimal platoon matchup against Yesavage, keeping his output in the marginal territory.",
